The Battery app is literally doing:

```java
Settings.System.putInt(..., "bypass_charge_state", state);
Settings.System.putInt(..., "bypass_charge_value", limit);
```

So your ADB commands are **officially equivalent** to changing the settings in the UI.

For future reference:

```bash
# Set charging limit
adb shell settings put system bypass_charge_value 80

# Read charging limit
adb shell settings get system bypass_charge_value

# Enable bypass charging
adb shell settings put system bypass_charge_state 1

# Disable bypass charging
adb shell settings put system bypass_charge_state 0

# Read state
adb shell settings get system bypass_charge_state
```

You can even make it a one-liner:

```bash
adb shell 'settings put system bypass_charge_value 80 && settings put system bypass_charge_state 1'
```

or disable it:

```bash
adb shell 'settings put system bypass_charge_state 0'
```

